From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windows.ui.xaml: ComboBox, ToggleSwitch, InputScope, CompositionTarget.Rendering, LayoutInformation

Windows Terminal's settings pages failed in their constructors: the Startup page's x:Name fields for its ComboBoxes and ToggleSwitches were null (no such types), so setting their automation names failed, and WinUI 2's NumberBox wanted InputScopeName; WinUI 2 also queues work for the next frame through CompositionTarget.Rendering and asks LayoutInformation for layout slots. ComboBox is drawn by us without a template, as the desktop's drop-down list: its selected item (through its ItemTemplate) beside a chevron, PlaceholderText when nothing is selected; a click, Enter, Space or F4 drops its items (ComboBoxItem containers) down in a popup window below it, a click on one selects it and closes the list, a click elsewhere closes it, Up and Down select on the box. ToggleSwitch is drawn as a switch with its Header and On/Off content; a click, Space or Enter flips it and raises Toggled. InputScope and InputScopeName are kept. CompositionTarget.Rendering and Rendered are raised every frame while they have handlers; LayoutInformation tells an element's layout slot and available size.
---
